From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:09:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [TEST] nb/intel/haswell: Program PEG AFE when MRC does not

peg_dmi_recipe() implements the PEG and DMI AFE (PHY) recipe, but only
the DMI half is ever used. MRC.bin programs the PEG AFE itself unless
the PEG devices are hidden from it, which HASWELL_HIDE_PEG_FROM_MRC
does by default so that the iGPU stays usable; its help text warns
that this "can make PEG devices unstable". Native raminit does not
program it either. In both cases the PEG link starts training with the
reset defaults. On the W541, the dGPU link reaches 8 GT/s x16 on the
OEM firmware.

Apply the PEG half of the recipe once, before starting link training
on the enabled PEG ports, with native raminit and when PEG is hidden
from MRC. It covers all eight bundles of the PEG PHY and already
writes the shared registers of all PEG functions. Build the recipe and
the VCU mailbox code for the MRC case too, and update the comment and
the help text that describe the missing AFE settings.

Not for upstream until tested on hardware: compare LnkSta (speed and
width) and the AER error counters of 00:01.0 and 01:00.0 under GPU load
with and without this change, with native raminit and with MRC.bin.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig     |  4 ++--
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Makefile.mk |  1 +
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_peg.c | 19 +++++++++++++++----
 3 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig
index 11950198a..908afe513 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig
@@ -117,8 +117,8 @@ config HASWELL_HIDE_PEG_FROM_MRC
 	help
 	  If set, hides all PEG devices from MRC. This allows the iGPU
 	  to be used even when a dedicated graphics card is present.
-	  However, it prevents MRC from programming PEG AFE registers,
-	  which can make PEG devices unstable. When unsure, choose N.
+	  MRC then does not program the PEG AFE registers, so coreboot
+	  programs them before starting PEG link training.
 
 # The UEFI System Agent binary needs to be at a fixed offset in the flash
 # and can therefore only reside in the COREBOOT fmap region
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Makefile.mk b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Makefile.mk
index c5cc82fc1..53f696f63 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Makefile.mk
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Makefile.mk
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@ romstage-y += early_dmi.c early_pcie.c vcu_mailbox.c
 subdirs-y  += broadwell_mrc
 
 else
+romstage-$(CONFIG_HASWELL_HIDE_PEG_FROM_MRC) += early_pcie.c vcu_mailbox.c
 subdirs-y  += haswell_mrc
 endif
 endif
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_peg.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_peg.c
index bb59d5d6d..c756b655d 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_peg.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_peg.c
@@ -32,10 +32,9 @@ static void start_peg2_link_training(const u8 func)
 	 *
 	 * If one really wants to enable the Intel iGPU as primary, hide
 	 * all PEG devices during MRC execution. This will trick the MRC
-	 * into thinking there aren't any, and will enable the IGD. Note
-	 * that PEG AFE settings will not be programmed, which may cause
-	 * stability problems at higher PCIe link speeds. The most ideal
-	 * way to fix this problem for good is to implement native init.
+	 * into thinking there aren't any, and will enable the IGD. MRC
+	 * then does not program the PEG AFE settings, which is done in
+	 * northbridge_setup_peg() instead.
 	 */
 	if (CONFIG(HASWELL_HIDE_PEG_FROM_MRC)) {
 		pci_and_config32(HOST_BRIDGE, DEVEN, ~deven_for_peg(func));
@@ -48,6 +47,18 @@ void northbridge_setup_peg(void)
 {
 	const u32 deven = pci_read_config32(HOST_BRIDGE, DEVEN);
 
+	/*
+	 * Program the PEG AFE settings before training the links. MRC does
+	 * this on its own, unless the PEG devices are hidden from it, and
+	 * native raminit does not. The recipe covers the whole PEG PHY, so
+	 * apply it once through PEG10.
+	 */
+	const bool program_afe = CONFIG(USE_NATIVE_RAMINIT) ||
+				 CONFIG(HASWELL_HIDE_PEG_FROM_MRC);
+
+	if (program_afe && (deven & DEVEN_D1F0EN))
+		peg_dmi_recipe(true, PEG_DEV(0));
+
 	for (u8 func = 0; func < MAX_PEG_FUNC; func++) {
 		if (deven & deven_for_peg(func)) {
 			start_peg2_link_training(func);
-- 
